<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<Workflow xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        THIS COMMENT SITS INSIDE THE ROOT ELEMENT DELIBERATELY. A comment placed ABOVE
        <Workflow> breaks `sf` deploy at source conversion with a misleading
        "unable to find matching parent xml file" error.

        NEW FILE, 2026-08-19. Disposition_Offer__c had no workflow metadata before this change.

        🔴 TWO FIELD UPDATES, NO WORKFLOW RULE. Both are fired ONLY by
        approvalProcesses/Disposition_Offer__c.Offer_Selection_Approval - Approved as its
        finalApprovalActions, Rejected as its finalRejectionActions. Do not add a <rules>
        element: an active rule writing Approval_Status__c would accept an offer and advance the
        parent Disposition on an ordinary edit.

        THE CHILD-OBJECT HALF OF D-1, exact twin of the BOV_Submission__c file. No Queueable is
        needed because Offer_Selection_Approval locks THIS OFFER, not the parent Disposition, so
        DispositionOfferTriggerHandler can update the parent synchronously with allOrNone = false
        in SYSTEM mode.

        ⚠ THE TRIGGER REQUIRES BOTH Approval_Status__c = Approved AND Is_Selected__c = true, and
        it requires the parent to be CURRENTLY on Offer Selection. Those are three distinct
        guards and none is redundant.

        🔴 REJECTION LEAVES THE DEAL AT Offer Selection, NOT AT Active Listing - AND THAT IS THE
        WHOLE POINT OF THE TWO-STEP DESIGN (D-3). Selecting the offer already advanced the
        Disposition by explicit service DML, before this approval ever ran. A rejected offer
        therefore parks the deal at Offer Selection for a re-pick instead of silently pretending
        no selection happened. The stage always tells the truth.

        ⚠ NAMING. agent-output/design-requirements.md section 6, open naming item 2, left the
        spelling open. Set_Offer_Approval_Approved / Set_Offer_Approval_Rejected is the chosen
        spelling and is used consistently here and in Offer_Selection_Approval. Nothing in Apex
        references a field update by name.

        DEPLOY ORDER - LOAD-BEARING. This file must land BEFORE
        approvalProcesses/Disposition_Offer__c.Offer_Selection_Approval, and both field updates
        require objects/Disposition_Offer__c/fields/Approval_Status__c.field-meta.xml.
    -->
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Set_Offer_Approval_Approved</fullName>
        <description>Final approval action of Offer_Selection_Approval. Sets Approval Status to Approved, which DispositionOfferTriggerHandler reads to accept the offer and move the parent Disposition from Offer Selection to LOI.</description>
        <field>Approval_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Approved</literalValue>
        <name>Set Offer Approval Approved</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
    <fieldUpdates>
        <fullName>Set_Offer_Approval_Rejected</fullName>
        <description>Final rejection action of Offer_Selection_Approval. Sets Approval Status to Rejected. No stage moves: the Disposition stays parked at Offer Selection so a different offer can be selected and submitted.</description>
        <field>Approval_Status__c</field>
        <literalValue>Rejected</literalValue>
        <name>Set Offer Approval Rejected</name>
        <notifyAssignee>false</notifyAssignee>
        <operation>Literal</operation>
        <protected>false</protected>
        <reevaluateOnChange>false</reevaluateOnChange>
    </fieldUpdates>
</Workflow>
